left to right direction
class "Job" as J <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + status: str
 + current_attempt_id: UUID
 + deleted_at: datetime | None
}
class "Attempt" as A <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + id: UUID
 + job_id: UUID
 + attempt_number: int
 + state: str
 + lease_token: UUID | None
 + lease_expires_at: datetime | None
 + deadline_at: datetime | None
}
class "RetryRequest" as R <<ORM>> $PROC {
 + job_id: UUID
 + request_id: UUID
 + attempt_id: UUID
}
class "Claim (lifecycle)" as C <<frozen dataclass>> $PROC {
 + job_id: UUID
 + attempt_id: UUID
 + lease_token: UUID
}
J "1" -- "1..*" A : job_id
J "0..1" --> "1" A : current_attempt_id
J "1" -- "0..*" R : unique(job_id,request_id)
R "0..1" --> "1" A : successor
C ..> A : frozen authority snapshot
legend bottom
+ public; - internal by Python convention; underlined = class/module scope.
Job/Attempt/RetryRequest are processing.models. Claim is processing.lifecycle; selected fields only.
Mapped[T] shown as T. Claim(A1,T1) cannot authorize A2. Mutating functions and task binding: W3-21/23.
